<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 17 July, from 1453 to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1453 CE <span class="tih-ago">573 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French artillery wins the Battle of Castillon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French cannon cut down an English army under John Talbot at Castillon in Gascony. It was the last battle of the Hundred Years' War, leaving Calais as England's only possession in France.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1762 CE <span class="tih-ago">264 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deposed Tsar Peter III dies in captivity</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after his wife Catherine seized the throne in a coup, Peter III died at Ropsha, almost certainly murdered by her supporters. Catherine the Great went on to rule Russia for 34 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 CE <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bolsheviks execute the Romanov family in Yekaterinburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the early hours, Nicholas II, his wife, their five children and four retainers were shot in the cellar of the Ipatiev House. Their remains were found decades later; the Orthodox Church canonised the family in 2000.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Potsdam Conference opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Truman, Stalin and Churchill, later replaced by Attlee, met at Cecilienhof near Berlin. They settled the occupation of Germany and issued the Potsdam Declaration demanding Japan's unconditional surrender.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1975 CE <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American and Soviet spacecraft dock in orbit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Apollo capsule docked with Soyuz 19, and Thomas Stafford and Alexei Leonov shook hands through the hatch. The first international crewed space mission was a landmark of Cold War détente.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1996 CE <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">TWA Flight 800 explodes off Long Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Boeing 747 bound for Paris exploded minutes after take-off from New York, killing all 230 on board. Investigators concluded that a spark had ignited fuel vapour in the centre wing tank.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
